    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d802">

                <pb facs="1030" n="916" xml:id="pg916"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">825.00 Revolutions/22: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Culbertson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-09-07T16:00:00-04:00">September 7, 1931—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 6 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>114. Navy Department states that it is in radio communication with the battleship
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Latorre</hi> and that it and the two remaining
                    mutinous ships have agreed to surrender. Details of surrender not yet known.</p>
                <p>Repeated Lima.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Culbertson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
